WEBVTT

00:00:00.917 --> 00:00:02.917
- Previously on The O. C:
- I want you out of my house.

00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:06.250
- Mom's kind of a train wreck.
- What kind of mother abandons her child?

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:08.708
- She has to come back, right?
- What happens if they don't find her?

00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:10.542
In the morning I'll take him
to Child Services.

00:00:10.708 --> 00:00:12.333
- Are you running away?
- Got a better idea?

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:15.125
- Where are we?
- One of my mom's housing developments.

00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:16.917
- How much do you need?
- It's $100,000.

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:20.125
- What are you doing with my girlfriend?
- Kill me and quit talking about it.

00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:24.625
Dude, this place is on fire.
We gotta go.

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:26.125
- I'm sorry.
- Ryan Atwood?

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.708
- We got some questions for you.
- It was an accident.

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.708
Then we got some questions
for you too.

00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:51.250
We gotta stop meeting like this.

00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:54.958
Some good news. Kirsten's company
has dropped all arson charges.

00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:58.917
Which means, pending your probation
hearing, you'll be out, no problem.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.042
When's that?

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.417
Thirty to 60 days.

00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:06.333
I could have you out sooner...

00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:10.042
...if I could release you into the care
of a parent or a guardian.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.208
- He gets to leave?
- Who, Luke?

00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:21.708
According to both of you,
the fire was an accident.

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:25.167
He's got no priors. His record's clean.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.458
And he has someone to take him home.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:33.458
Ryan, you know, if I could...

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.042
It's gonna be okay.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.458
My mom ditched me, I burned your wife's
house down, how is this gonna be okay?

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.458
- We'll find your mother.
- And what if we don't?

00:01:48.625 --> 00:01:51.042
- We will do whatever it takes.
- I mean...

00:01:51.125 --> 00:01:53.542
...what if I don't want to find her?

00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:58.750
If only you'd come to me
instead of running away.

00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:01.333
So I could end up
in Child Services and foster care?

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.042
- You could have died in that fire.
- Look...

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.000
...you've done more than enough.
I can take care of myself.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.000
Won't be that different
from how it's been.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.667
We'll talk again before your hearing.

00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:17.792
Tell your wife thanks.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.458
Already did.

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:27.750
Step back.

00:02:36.375 --> 00:02:38.167
Sorry.

00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:41.333
You ain't now, but you will be.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.708
Now all we need are the Bellinis.
And can you make mine a double?

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:33.833
Wow. You're all set up for
your Newpsie convention.

00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:35.917
Hey, when do these vultures land?

00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:40.125
Soon. And I'm sure that I have
a doily out of place somewhere.

00:03:40.292 --> 00:03:42.125
Good. Gives them something
to talk about.

00:03:42.292 --> 00:03:44.917
I don't know why you have them over.
You don't like them.

00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:47.083
I don't don't like them.
I grew up with them.

00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:50.083
They're my oldest friends.
Besides, it's for charity.

00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:52.500
What's on the agenda?
What are you dragging me to?

00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:55.083
Casino Night.

00:03:55.292 --> 00:03:58.083
This home-from-the-office
housewife thing, it's really...

00:03:58.208 --> 00:04:00.208
- Disturbing?
- Hot.

00:04:00.375 --> 00:04:02.792
Disturbingly hot.

00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:08.792
Hey. What you doing?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.750
Nothing. I'm grounded.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.250
Well, you're handling it well.

00:04:13.417 --> 00:04:15.750
You're lucky you're only grounded.

00:04:19.708 --> 00:04:21.208
You gonna see him?

00:04:21.417 --> 00:04:24.125
Ryan? No. There's nothing
I can do for him right now.

00:04:24.333 --> 00:04:26.333
Yeah? You think he's okay?

00:04:27.208 --> 00:04:30.333
There's a reason why I like to try
to keep kids out of those places.

00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:32.917
You can't get him out?
You're just not a good enough lawyer?

00:04:33.125 --> 00:04:36.708
- My hands are tied until we find his mom.
- So then why can't he stay here?

00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:39.417
I will not have this conversation again.

00:04:39.625 --> 00:04:41.708
Rosa, can you make sure
that the scones go inside?

00:04:41.917 --> 00:04:45.208
If anything happens to Ryan, it's on
you, so I hope you can live with that.

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:49.083
What I can't live with is if something
was to happen to you because of him.

00:04:49.292 --> 00:04:52.042
- Like I meet someone who doesn't suck?
- We're not his parents.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.542
- I am not his mother.
- Good thing.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.250
Hey. Get back here. Apologize.

00:05:05.125 --> 00:05:08.542
- Ladies.
- Sandy, hi, how are you?

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.833
Are you holding up okay?
That poor boy.

00:05:11.042 --> 00:05:13.042
- He's locked up, yes?
- Yeah, temporarily.

00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:16.833
Well, nobody blames you for bringing him
into the community. You're so trusting.

00:05:19.042 --> 00:05:22.542
Hey, Julie. Their house looks good.
I thought you said it burned down.

00:05:22.625 --> 00:05:26.833
Not this one, one of Kirsten's
developments. Luckily, she has so many.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.000
Well, I should be off.

00:05:30.208 --> 00:05:32.917
Gotta find the next kid
to jeopardize the community.

00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:35.750
Maybe a black kid. Or an Asian kid.

00:05:35.958 --> 00:05:37.167
Bye, ladies.

00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:41.542
- How about a Bellini?
- Yes!

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.167
Look at this food!

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:59.458
Who's sorry now? You got a problem?
You disrespecting me?

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.750
As long as you here,
you best watch out for me, man.

00:06:11.542 --> 00:06:16.167
I think it's an embarrassment that we still
don't have a theme for the fundraiser.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:19.167
- Well, it's Casino Night.
- I thought it was Monte Carlo Night.

00:06:19.375 --> 00:06:22.375
- No, it's Vegas Night.
- See, this is a travesty.

00:06:22.583 --> 00:06:25.667
It can't be Monte Carlo Night.
Cotillion is coming up.

00:06:25.875 --> 00:06:29.667
Don't you remember our amendment? No
two black-tie events in the same month.

00:06:29.792 --> 00:06:31.375
I'll be right back.

00:06:31.583 --> 00:06:33.583
I have to go...

00:06:34.083 --> 00:06:35.958
...check on the thing.

00:06:40.042 --> 00:06:44.042
She's been through so much.
Her son was friends with that boy.

00:07:09.583 --> 00:07:11.792
Where do you think you're going?

00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:18.167
- What are you doing out here?
- I'm taking a break. Where are you going?

00:07:18.375 --> 00:07:20.792
- I'm not going anywhere.
- Seth.

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:24.167
I'm going to juvie to visit Ryan.

00:07:24.375 --> 00:07:26.375
No. No, you're not. No way.

00:07:26.875 --> 00:07:28.958
- Okay. Bye.
- Seth.

00:07:30.167 --> 00:07:33.083
I know that I am not the
perfect Carol Brady mom...

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.667
...but I love you,
and I am trying to protect you.

00:07:35.875 --> 00:07:39.125
I have dropped all the charges. I have
hired somebody to find his mother.

00:07:39.333 --> 00:07:41.917
What more do you want?

00:07:46.292 --> 00:07:49.000
I would like you to go with me.

00:07:49.208 --> 00:07:51.417
Kirsten? Oh, there you are.

00:07:51.625 --> 00:07:53.917
We're talking about the bunting.
Is acetate okay?

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.792
- Sounds great.
- Okay.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.917
Give me 15 minutes to lose the ladies.

00:08:05.708 --> 00:08:07.000
Can I try this on?

00:08:07.083 --> 00:08:08.792
Summer, my dad's home, you know.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.583
You say that like it's a bad thing.

00:08:10.792 --> 00:08:12.292
Oh, gross!

00:08:12.375 --> 00:08:14.500
Your dad's always home these days.
What's up?

00:08:15.167 --> 00:08:18.792
Hey, Luke, it's me. I just...

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.750
...wanted to talk. So call me.

00:08:22.625 --> 00:08:23.833
Please.

00:08:24.042 --> 00:08:25.833
Still hasn't called you back?

00:08:25.917 --> 00:08:28.042
He was in lockup.
Maybe he's into dudes now.

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:33.125
God, he loves you. He got in a fight
and burnt a house down over you.

00:08:33.333 --> 00:08:35.417
That's hot. What more do you need?

00:08:35.625 --> 00:08:37.625
- How about talking to me?
- He'll get over it.

00:08:38.333 --> 00:08:40.625
He can't really think
you're into that Chino kid.

00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:45.125
So how's your mother?

00:08:45.292 --> 00:08:47.708
Just... married.

00:08:48.625 --> 00:08:51.125
Marissa, you've got company.

00:08:53.083 --> 00:08:55.708
- Oh, my God.
- Sorry.

00:08:55.917 --> 00:08:59.583
Hi, Summer. I'm... I'm... I'm Seth Cohen.
I live... I live right next door.

00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:03.042
What's up?

00:09:04.042 --> 00:09:05.542
What?

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:07.542
Yes, what is up.

00:09:08.667 --> 00:09:12.458
I'm going to visit Ryan. I thought maybe
you'd like to come. He'd love to see you.

00:09:12.542 --> 00:09:17.333
What's that, Seth? Did you say you need
a ride to a Star Wars convention?

00:09:17.625 --> 00:09:21.833
Star Wars? I'm sorry, her top was off.
You couldn't have at least said X- Men?

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:27.208
I can't go with you. I can't see Ryan.
I mean, Luke's not talking to me as it is.

00:09:27.417 --> 00:09:30.042
So what? Ryan's in jail.
I thought we were all friends.

00:09:30.125 --> 00:09:33.417
It's just... It's too complicated.

00:09:33.625 --> 00:09:35.125
- To visit him?
- I can't, okay?

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.333
Yeah, fine. Whatever.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.542
Let's just make this quick, okay?

00:10:32.958 --> 00:10:35.292
Kirsten and Seth Cohen.

00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:43.583
Hey.

00:10:45.083 --> 00:10:47.083
- What happened to your neck?
- It's nothing.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.875
- You okay?
- Great.

00:10:52.667 --> 00:10:54.375
So I'm sorry the plan didn't work.

00:10:56.167 --> 00:10:59.750
I thought I had it figured out.
I thought you were safe. I was wrong.

00:10:59.833 --> 00:11:02.833
What's the matter? Give me a smile.

00:11:07.083 --> 00:11:11.000
So Marissa seemed pretty weird
when I tried to talk to her.

00:11:11.208 --> 00:11:14.792
- What happened between you guys?
- You got a nice swerve on you. You fine.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.375
- Hey, leave her alone.
- Ryan, it's okay.

00:11:17.583 --> 00:11:19.208
Are you joking? Is this your honey?

00:11:19.375 --> 00:11:21.375
Come here, bitch,
I wanna get a look at you.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.167
- Seth, let's go, now.
- I only need two minutes.

00:11:24.375 --> 00:11:25.667
- Leave her alone.
- Seth, now.

00:11:25.875 --> 00:11:27.375
- What you gonna do?
- Guards!

00:11:28.667 --> 00:11:29.667
Guards!

00:11:31.958 --> 00:11:33.792
I'll kill you, punk!

00:11:39.083 --> 00:11:41.875
You're dead! You hear me?
You're dead!

00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:06.000
Seth, what did we say?
No video games.

00:12:13.792 --> 00:12:15.792
I never knew you
to be an impulse shopper.

00:12:15.875 --> 00:12:17.375
I didn't know what else to do.

00:12:17.583 --> 00:12:20.083
- Did you tell him it was permanent?
- No, of course not.

00:12:20.375 --> 00:12:24.292
We can't jerk him around, pulling him
out of juvie, sending him to foster care...

00:12:24.375 --> 00:12:27.083
...giving him hope and taking it away.

00:12:27.167 --> 00:12:30.750
They were gonna kill him in that place.
He couldn't stay there.

00:12:30.917 --> 00:12:34.625
But he can't stay here.
We've got to find his mother.

00:12:34.833 --> 00:12:36.917
- He doesn't want to find her.
- He's a kid.

00:12:37.125 --> 00:12:38.833
He doesn't know what he wants.

00:12:39.042 --> 00:12:41.042
So I guess I won't unpack.

00:12:57.208 --> 00:12:58.917
Hey.

00:13:00.125 --> 00:13:02.917
Help yourself to a wide assortment
of breakfast cereals.

00:13:07.417 --> 00:13:09.708
So, Ryan, what...?

00:13:10.375 --> 00:13:13.833
What exactly happened that night with
Marissa before Luke showed up?

00:13:14.042 --> 00:13:16.167
- She came to see me.
- And?

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.958
- And I told her to leave.
- You asked her to leave?

00:13:19.542 --> 00:13:22.542
That's it? You two were up there
all alone and you expect me...?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:25.250
I thought I was taking off
in the morning.

00:13:25.958 --> 00:13:28.750
- It didn't seem right.
- You're still here. She's next door.

00:13:29.417 --> 00:13:32.125
I don't know. I said some things.

00:13:32.333 --> 00:13:34.333
So now's your chance to take it back.

00:13:36.542 --> 00:13:39.542
Hey. I'm off.
They're waiting for me in the ballroom.

00:13:39.625 --> 00:13:41.833
Those ladies can't do anything
unless I'm there.

00:13:42.042 --> 00:13:43.833
Hey, you should come. It'll be fun.

00:13:43.917 --> 00:13:46.500
Well, not fun, but it's for charity.

00:13:47.125 --> 00:13:48.500
No, thanks.

00:13:48.708 --> 00:13:51.125
Marissa, honey, enough moping.

00:13:51.333 --> 00:13:54.667
It's sweet that you're so concerned about
this boy, but he's in the system now.

00:13:54.875 --> 00:13:56.375
He's being taken care of.

00:13:56.583 --> 00:13:59.458
And he's not your responsibility
because he's in love with you.

00:13:59.667 --> 00:14:01.667
He's not in love with me.

00:14:01.875 --> 00:14:04.875
Why not?
He thinks he's too good for you?

00:14:04.958 --> 00:14:07.958
Actually, he thinks
I'm too good for him.

00:14:08.167 --> 00:14:10.750
Well, he's right. But that's the past.

00:14:10.958 --> 00:14:15.167
And you need to focus on the future,
which means Luke.

00:14:15.333 --> 00:14:17.542
You've invested so much
with Luke, honey.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.125
Your relationship has
too much potential...

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.542
...to be squandered by
some silly misunderstanding.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:28.750
So finish your hair, put on a nice top
and please come join me at the club.

00:14:30.125 --> 00:14:32.833
Okay. Thanks, Mom.

00:14:33.417 --> 00:14:35.167
That's what I'm here for.

00:14:37.375 --> 00:14:41.083
I have to make some calls, so if you
could finish up, that would be terrific.

00:14:41.167 --> 00:14:43.083
Where are you going?

00:14:43.292 --> 00:14:47.292
I've got an early court date,
then I'm in and out of the office.

00:14:47.375 --> 00:14:50.375
I have to set up for Casino Night.
What about Ryan?

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:53.250
I called the private investigator
about his mother.

00:14:53.375 --> 00:14:55.583
Yeah, but what am I
supposed to do with him?

00:14:56.375 --> 00:14:58.375
Take him with you.
Spend some time together.

00:14:58.458 --> 00:15:01.875
- With all those women there?
- Sure. They'll love him.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:13.042
- Hi, Julie.
- Kirsten, Seth.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.667
Julie, this is Ryan.

00:15:15.625 --> 00:15:18.000
I'm Julie Cooper.
I've heard so much about you.

00:15:18.708 --> 00:15:21.583
- Nice to meet you too.
- There he is.

00:15:22.917 --> 00:15:25.208
Hey, Mrs. Cooper. How you doing?

00:15:25.375 --> 00:15:28.208
- Hey, Luke.
- Hi, Luke. Thanks for coming.

00:15:28.375 --> 00:15:32.292
You know, anything I can do to help
make amends for what happened.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.000
Luke, it's good to see you.

00:15:34.167 --> 00:15:37.167
Ryan, I forgot that he was coming.
If you wanna...

00:15:37.292 --> 00:15:39.500
No, I'm here. How can I help?

00:15:39.958 --> 00:15:44.458
Well, now that we have our big, strong,
strapping men, time for heavy lifting.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.875
Hey. I was hoping maybe we could talk.

00:15:57.458 --> 00:15:59.500
Which one of us did you want to talk to?

00:15:59.625 --> 00:16:00.917
Luke, come on.

00:16:08.125 --> 00:16:12.792
Sorry. I feel like ever since I've
gotten here, I've screwed everything up.

00:16:12.917 --> 00:16:15.583
No, I'm sorry. It's my fault too.

00:16:15.792 --> 00:16:18.583
I mean, I never should have left Luke
to see you that night.

00:16:18.792 --> 00:16:22.583
- And those things you said before...
- I didn't... What I said...

00:16:22.792 --> 00:16:25.875
You were right.
We're from two different worlds.

00:16:27.375 --> 00:16:29.500
I'm glad you're okay.

00:16:42.833 --> 00:16:45.833
Okay. What happened
up at that house with me and her...

00:16:46.042 --> 00:16:49.917
I don't want to hear about it. You and I
have nothing to say to each other.

00:16:50.542 --> 00:16:53.417
I don't know who you are
or what you're doing here.

00:16:53.542 --> 00:16:56.333
All I know is, you and me, we're done.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:17:00.625
Okay, boys. Ryan, why don't you
come with me. New project.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.917
- Thank you.
- How dare they?

00:17:12.083 --> 00:17:14.292
This boy is violent. He's a menace.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:18.917
They may forgive and forget, but I don't.
Who's to say he won't do it again?

00:17:19.083 --> 00:17:21.042
You're right. You are right.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:23.667
The police are taking
criminals off the street...

00:17:23.833 --> 00:17:26.167
...and Sandy Cohen is putting them
in my back yard.

00:17:26.333 --> 00:17:28.542
- How does she put up with it?
- Who, Kirsten?

00:17:28.625 --> 00:17:31.958
She's never home. She's always
working, building her empire.

00:17:32.125 --> 00:17:33.458
I feel sorry for her.

00:17:33.625 --> 00:17:36.125
Dr. Phil did a show on mothers
who avoid home life...

00:17:36.333 --> 00:17:38.833
...by becoming workaholics. So sad.

00:17:38.917 --> 00:17:43.250
I just hope she has a vault and she keeps
her jewels locked up. She has expensive...

00:17:43.417 --> 00:17:46.042
Hey, ladies. Care if I join you?

00:17:50.042 --> 00:17:51.625
You mind?

00:17:52.833 --> 00:17:55.208
So I couldn't help but overhear.

00:17:55.333 --> 00:17:59.333
- I... Well, I hope that you're not...
- Mad? Offended? No.

00:17:59.833 --> 00:18:03.583
I am disappointed.
And frankly, I'm a little surprised.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:06.458
This is supposed to be a community
that welcomes outsiders.

00:18:06.667 --> 00:18:10.958
I mean, me, I'm all the way from the
Bronx. And you're from Riverside, right?

00:18:11.167 --> 00:18:14.667
Which is not that different from
where Ryan's from. Excuse me a minute.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:16.750
Hello?

00:18:18.333 --> 00:18:20.333
Yeah. Dawn. That's her.

00:18:23.667 --> 00:18:25.667
Good job.

00:18:25.833 --> 00:18:27.542
Okay. Bye.

00:18:31.333 --> 00:18:33.125
Thanks for the muffin.

00:18:37.833 --> 00:18:39.417
Can I have a napkin? Now?

00:18:39.625 --> 00:18:44.042
What am I supposed to do
with 120,000 pounds of concrete?

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.000
Get a new mixer.

00:18:49.167 --> 00:18:50.500
Just call me when you know.

00:18:51.875 --> 00:18:54.292
What do you do exactly?
Real estate or construction?

00:18:54.458 --> 00:18:55.792
Dude, don't ask.

00:18:55.875 --> 00:18:59.667
I tried to explain it to Seth once,
and he fell asleep halfway through.

00:18:59.875 --> 00:19:03.083
Okay. But...
Yeah, that's pretty much true.

00:19:04.667 --> 00:19:06.250
Try me.

00:19:07.375 --> 00:19:10.958
My dad is in real-estate development.
He owns the Newport Group.

00:19:11.167 --> 00:19:13.042
Wow. You guys built the mall?

00:19:13.167 --> 00:19:15.667
Civic auditorium? Baseball stadium?
Stuff like that?

00:19:15.875 --> 00:19:17.667
I'm in charge of residential development.

00:19:18.167 --> 00:19:21.542
So you deal with contractors, architects,
planning and zoning commission?

00:19:21.667 --> 00:19:24.250
- How'd you know?
- I worked construction a couple summers.

00:19:24.458 --> 00:19:27.000
And I used to want to be an architect.

00:19:28.583 --> 00:19:31.208
- And what do you want to be now?
- Seventeen.

00:19:33.208 --> 00:19:34.375
Me too.

00:19:39.792 --> 00:19:42.667
Hey. I thought you were setting up at...

00:19:44.083 --> 00:19:46.667
You will not believe
what Sandy Cohen said to me.

00:19:46.792 --> 00:19:50.583
He basically called me white trash.
He said I was from Riverside.

00:19:50.792 --> 00:19:52.875
Honey, you are from Riverside.

00:19:53.375 --> 00:19:54.875
It was his tone.

00:19:55.083 --> 00:19:57.958
Compare me to that boy,
and to bring him to our function...

00:19:58.167 --> 00:20:01.875
Kirsten is out of control.
She thinks the rules don't apply to her?

00:20:01.958 --> 00:20:05.083
I know you were young, but how you ever
dated that woman, I can't understand.

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:08.500
- I have half a mind to call and tell her...
- Leave Kirsten alone.

00:20:11.125 --> 00:20:12.833
She's the one paying our bills.

00:20:14.417 --> 00:20:16.292
What are you talking about?

00:20:16.708 --> 00:20:21.500
You know that problem
I was having at work? Well...

00:20:22.125 --> 00:20:23.500
...she solved it.

00:20:25.083 --> 00:20:29.208
You went to Kirsten for a handout?
How do you think this makes us look?

00:20:29.417 --> 00:20:33.292
- I wouldn't really call it a handout.
- Oh, really? What would you call it?

00:20:36.208 --> 00:20:38.375
A hundred thousand dollars.

00:20:48.542 --> 00:20:50.125
That machine ate my change.

00:20:50.333 --> 00:20:53.250
Okay, okay. That one's always broken.

00:20:53.417 --> 00:20:55.917
Here you go. Try the next one over.

00:20:58.042 --> 00:21:00.833
Dawn Atwood?
Sandy Cohen, Ryan's attorney.

00:21:03.208 --> 00:21:06.417
- I'd love to talk to you.
- I can't talk.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:10.417
- This stupid thing's stuck.
- It'll only take a couple of minutes.

00:21:11.125 --> 00:21:13.000
Damn it!

00:21:18.125 --> 00:21:19.417
How is he?

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:23.708
Why don't we grab a cup of coffee
and talk about it?

00:21:31.458 --> 00:21:35.542
There's some historical homes in the area.
We can go on an architectural tour.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:39.542
- Yeah, those things are awesome.
- Yeah, I'd like that.

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:52.417
Hey, Ry.

00:22:00.208 --> 00:22:01.833
Thank you, Rosa.

00:22:07.625 --> 00:22:09.417
Thanks.

00:22:09.625 --> 00:22:11.125
No, thank you.

00:22:18.958 --> 00:22:21.750
So, Dawn, how long you been
working at the Laundromat?

00:22:21.958 --> 00:22:24.250
Not long. Just a couple weeks.

00:22:24.375 --> 00:22:27.833
- What happened to the restaurant?
- They were making cutbacks.

00:22:28.042 --> 00:22:29.542
You got fired.

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:32.458
Well, it was for the best.

00:22:32.542 --> 00:22:36.458
They had rats, cockroaches. Disgusting.

00:22:38.458 --> 00:22:40.042
You seen Trey?

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:43.625
I went to visit him at the prison.
He wouldn't see me.

00:22:47.917 --> 00:22:52.333
- Where are you living these days?
- With friends. I'm between places now.

00:22:53.417 --> 00:22:56.000
- Why don't you stay here tonight?
- What about A.J.?

00:22:57.875 --> 00:23:00.500
No. I broke up with him.

00:23:01.083 --> 00:23:02.875
We're through.

00:23:03.083 --> 00:23:04.667
No more.

00:23:06.792 --> 00:23:08.292
I put up with too much.

00:23:10.458 --> 00:23:13.958
He laid his hands on me
and Ryan too many times.

00:23:14.167 --> 00:23:16.875
- Mom.
- What?

00:23:17.083 --> 00:23:18.875
I'm just saying...

00:23:19.542 --> 00:23:21.750
...he was a bad influence, you know.

00:23:21.958 --> 00:23:24.458
- With his drinking...
- Because A.J. Was the problem.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:29.542
Hey, I haven't touched a drop
since I dumped his sorry ass last week.

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:32.958
The scum he used to bring
into the house, his whole coke thing...

00:23:33.833 --> 00:23:37.208
- Where you going?
- It was bad enough living it the first time.

00:23:37.417 --> 00:23:39.208
Ryan. Wait, sweetie.

00:23:39.708 --> 00:23:41.000
Sorry.

00:23:51.292 --> 00:23:54.083
- Will you at least talk to me?
- What are you even doing here?

00:23:54.292 --> 00:23:57.083
I came for you.

00:23:57.292 --> 00:23:59.583
Why? What do you want from me?

00:24:00.292 --> 00:24:01.667
You left a note.

00:24:03.375 --> 00:24:04.792
- A note.
- Let me explain...

00:24:04.875 --> 00:24:07.375
You abandoned me.
You threw me out. You just took off.

00:24:07.583 --> 00:24:09.958
I know, honey. I was...

00:24:10.875 --> 00:24:14.375
And A.J. And the drinking and...

00:24:17.833 --> 00:24:20.417
It's gonna be different now.

00:24:20.917 --> 00:24:24.125
That's what you said when we moved
from Fresno after Dad got arrested.

00:24:24.208 --> 00:24:26.208
I'm gonna be different now.

00:24:26.417 --> 00:24:29.000
We have a chance to start over, babe.

00:24:29.125 --> 00:24:33.000
We've never had people like them,
you know, who wanted to help us.

00:24:33.208 --> 00:24:34.292
Right.

00:24:34.500 --> 00:24:38.000
Someone offers you a nice place to stay,
suddenly you're all about the mom thing.

00:24:42.792 --> 00:24:45.875
I didn't know what I was doing
when I married your dad.

00:24:46.083 --> 00:24:48.792
I was too young
when I had your brother.

00:24:49.292 --> 00:24:50.875
But with you...

00:24:53.375 --> 00:24:56.167
You were always the smart one,
you know?

00:24:57.792 --> 00:24:59.417
The good one.

00:25:00.417 --> 00:25:02.917
When you got arrested...

00:25:05.125 --> 00:25:07.542
...I knew I'd failed, and...

00:25:09.708 --> 00:25:12.042
...you were my last hope.

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:17.833
I should go.

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.500
Wait.

00:25:28.292 --> 00:25:30.500
You ever gonna forgive me, kiddo?

00:25:35.583 --> 00:25:37.917
Let's just go slow, huh?

00:25:40.542 --> 00:25:41.833
Okay.

00:25:44.958 --> 00:25:46.750
Whatever you want.

00:25:49.125 --> 00:25:50.958
I'm not gonna lose you again.

00:25:57.250 --> 00:26:00.917
- So where did they go, anyways?
- I don't know. Out.

00:26:01.125 --> 00:26:03.625
All right. So we'll just
wait for happy hour to end.

00:26:03.708 --> 00:26:07.208
Seth, we need to be supportive.
She seems like she's trying.

00:26:07.333 --> 00:26:09.125
Yeah, but how do you know?

00:26:09.333 --> 00:26:13.125
I mean, this woman abandoned him,
and now all she has to do is show up?

00:26:13.333 --> 00:26:16.333
Come on. She should be the one
that's on probation, not Ryan.

00:26:16.500 --> 00:26:19.000
You want me to invite her to stay
so we can watch her?

00:26:19.125 --> 00:26:21.583
Yes, that is exactly
what I want you to do.

00:26:26.375 --> 00:26:28.375
What a beautiful walk.

00:26:28.542 --> 00:26:30.250
The water's so warm.

00:26:30.375 --> 00:26:32.375
Not that Ryan would know.

00:26:32.542 --> 00:26:36.250
- You used to love going in the water.
- Not with all my clothes on.

00:26:36.458 --> 00:26:37.958
I'm an embarrassment to my son.

00:26:38.167 --> 00:26:40.167
Welcome to my world.

00:26:41.333 --> 00:26:44.542
Well, we should probably
head out soon.

00:26:45.625 --> 00:26:50.125
Actually, I was thinking. You just
got here, you have nowhere to stay.

00:26:50.458 --> 00:26:52.458
We're all just getting to know
each other.

00:26:52.625 --> 00:26:54.333
- We're having a party tonight.
- Right.

00:26:54.417 --> 00:26:56.542
Not for me. But thanks, though.

00:26:56.750 --> 00:26:59.750
- Vegas Night.
- Vegas, huh?

00:27:00.333 --> 00:27:03.875
It's very kind of you to offer,
but I don't have anything to wear.

00:27:04.083 --> 00:27:05.792
We'll find something.

00:27:16.958 --> 00:27:18.583
Kirsten does the same thing.

00:27:18.750 --> 00:27:21.750
Washes the dishes before
putting them in the dishwasher.

00:27:21.958 --> 00:27:24.750
I never know whether
they're clean or dirty.

00:27:24.958 --> 00:27:27.042
We never had a dishwasher.

00:27:27.750 --> 00:27:30.750
- So how's everything going?
- Okay, I guess.

00:27:31.042 --> 00:27:32.958
We had a good day.

00:27:34.458 --> 00:27:38.250
You being with your mother doesn't mean
we're not gonna still see each other.

00:27:38.458 --> 00:27:40.250
She really likes it here.

00:27:40.458 --> 00:27:44.042
She talked about finding
someplace small nearby.

00:27:44.250 --> 00:27:46.208
In the numbered streets.

00:27:47.083 --> 00:27:48.417
So...

00:27:49.792 --> 00:27:51.208
...how do I look?

00:28:10.292 --> 00:28:12.458
All their parties like this?

00:28:12.583 --> 00:28:14.583
Pretty much.

00:28:14.792 --> 00:28:18.375
Well, let's clean them out, kid.

00:28:22.250 --> 00:28:24.083
- Kirsten.
- Excuse me.

00:28:24.250 --> 00:28:26.167
Another perfect event.

00:28:26.333 --> 00:28:28.500
So business is good?

00:28:28.708 --> 00:28:30.125
Yeah, it's good.

00:28:30.333 --> 00:28:33.125
- I love your dress.
- You do? It's yours.

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:36.500
- Hi.
- Hey. How are you?

00:28:36.708 --> 00:28:38.708
- Good to see you.
- Yeah.

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:41.917
- Would you like a drink?
- I'd love one.

00:28:44.583 --> 00:28:47.792
- It's all fabulous. Just fabulous.
- Thank you.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:51.500
How much did you get for the hug?

00:29:02.083 --> 00:29:03.667
Betting kind of big, Mom?

00:29:03.875 --> 00:29:07.083
It's for charity.
Besides, the count's way positive.

00:29:07.292 --> 00:29:10.250
You're counting?
It's not a single deck.

00:29:10.333 --> 00:29:12.750
Oh, honey, if I teach you
anything in this world...

00:29:12.917 --> 00:29:15.417
...the count goes way higher
with multiple decks.

00:29:16.208 --> 00:29:18.125
Blackjack.

00:29:19.417 --> 00:29:22.417
See, honey?
My luck's turning around already.

00:29:26.625 --> 00:29:28.125
Yes!

00:29:29.708 --> 00:29:31.208
That's beautiful.

00:29:31.417 --> 00:29:34.500
I told you we could do it. I told you too!

00:29:42.708 --> 00:29:46.292
Excuse me.
Tonic water and lime, please?

00:29:51.958 --> 00:29:53.542
My boy.

00:29:53.750 --> 00:29:56.542
Lucky for him, he's got my brains.

00:30:03.333 --> 00:30:04.750
Go.

00:30:04.917 --> 00:30:07.333
Have fun with your friend.

00:30:07.542 --> 00:30:10.333
I'll be fine.
You don't have to babysit me.

00:30:34.958 --> 00:30:37.375
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:30:38.875 --> 00:30:40.667
So is that your mom?

00:30:42.042 --> 00:30:43.458
Yeah.

00:30:44.167 --> 00:30:47.750
She came back, so I guess
that means you're going home.

00:30:48.542 --> 00:30:50.458
Yeah, I guess.

00:30:50.958 --> 00:30:53.250
Well, good luck with everything.

00:30:53.458 --> 00:30:55.958
You too. Have a nice life.

00:31:03.917 --> 00:31:05.625
You should go.

00:31:23.292 --> 00:31:25.167
Hi, Summer. Seth Cohen.

00:31:25.292 --> 00:31:27.375
I'm superstitious. Blow on these.

00:31:27.958 --> 00:31:29.958
- What?
- Blow.

00:31:36.750 --> 00:31:39.875
We're good! Do it again.

00:31:42.750 --> 00:31:44.958
- You're not going anywhere, Syd.
- Seth.

00:31:45.167 --> 00:31:46.667
- Whatever.
- Okay.

00:31:46.833 --> 00:31:48.542
Blow.

00:31:50.833 --> 00:31:53.042
You can't just not talk to me.

00:31:54.042 --> 00:31:55.500
Watch me.

00:31:56.000 --> 00:32:00.500
It's not like you're innocent in all this.
I mean, you didn't have to attack him.

00:32:00.708 --> 00:32:03.000
What was I supposed to do?

00:32:03.292 --> 00:32:06.000
You left me to go up there for him.

00:32:07.375 --> 00:32:09.000
It's not like that.

00:32:09.208 --> 00:32:11.167
It was a mistake.

00:32:12.167 --> 00:32:13.792
Hell, yeah.

00:32:19.583 --> 00:32:22.667
- Hi, Sandy.
- Hey, Julie.

00:32:22.875 --> 00:32:27.167
I came to apologize and say thank you.
The check that you guys gave Jimmy.

00:32:27.750 --> 00:32:30.583
You never know who your friends are
until you're in need.

00:32:30.750 --> 00:32:32.250
And we needed that 100 grand.

00:32:34.083 --> 00:32:36.500
It was our pleasure.
You can't take it with you.

00:32:42.708 --> 00:32:45.208
- Hi.
- What do you want?

00:32:45.292 --> 00:32:48.000
Nothing happened
with Marissa and me.

00:32:48.208 --> 00:32:51.000
- I don't want to talk about it.
- Listen.

00:32:52.417 --> 00:32:56.208
She chose you.
You're the one she wants.

00:33:15.167 --> 00:33:17.375
Can I get a 7 and 7, please?

00:33:17.583 --> 00:33:19.333
Nerves. Tough game of poker.

00:33:21.333 --> 00:33:23.125
Thank you.

00:33:23.250 --> 00:33:27.333
- Want some dessert?
- Yeah, we could have a little piece.

00:33:28.208 --> 00:33:30.417
Always does the trick.

00:33:45.208 --> 00:33:47.500
You rock, Stanley.

00:33:58.000 --> 00:33:59.500
Hey.

00:34:00.667 --> 00:34:02.458
Let's try again.

00:34:13.542 --> 00:34:16.417
Oh, crap. My damn luck, huh?

00:34:17.542 --> 00:34:21.625
Well, pony up, honey. Don't be shy.

00:34:26.208 --> 00:34:28.833
My new best friend. Thank you.

00:34:35.500 --> 00:34:37.500
Don't you think you've had enough?

00:34:39.125 --> 00:34:40.708
You're right.

00:34:41.083 --> 00:34:43.583
Just gotta learn to celebrate
without the sauce.

00:34:44.458 --> 00:34:46.875
Well, no one said it was
going to be easy.

00:34:47.750 --> 00:34:50.542
Could we talk? It's important.

00:34:50.667 --> 00:34:52.542
Of course. Excuse us.

00:34:52.750 --> 00:34:54.042
Sure.

00:35:05.833 --> 00:35:08.833
- You want to hear something so funny?
- Always.

00:35:09.042 --> 00:35:12.542
Sandy Cohen had no idea
Kirsten wrote you that check.

00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:17.125
Imagine being so rich you don't tell your
husband you're giving away $100,000.

00:35:17.333 --> 00:35:19.542
Right. You know what?

00:35:19.750 --> 00:35:22.208
Who needs chips? You got Kirsten.

00:35:23.042 --> 00:35:24.375
What did you say to him?

00:35:24.500 --> 00:35:27.083
You don't care how this makes me feel,
that you went to her.

00:35:27.292 --> 00:35:29.583
I had no choice.
You didn't want to talk about it.

00:35:29.792 --> 00:35:31.583
I was trying to save us.

00:35:31.792 --> 00:35:34.167
Our family was in trouble.

00:35:35.083 --> 00:35:36.667
Looks like we're not the only ones.

00:35:38.083 --> 00:35:40.958
A hundred thousand dollars!
That's more than I make in a year.

00:35:41.875 --> 00:35:44.250
It's just a loan...

00:35:44.375 --> 00:35:45.875
...of my money.

00:35:45.958 --> 00:35:48.375
It's not the money.
It's that you never told me.

00:35:49.042 --> 00:35:50.875
I know.

00:35:50.958 --> 00:35:53.167
- I don't know why.
- I got a couple of ideas.

00:35:53.375 --> 00:35:56.667
Let me take you on a journey through
my neuroses for the past hour or so.

00:35:56.833 --> 00:35:59.833
Sandy, I promise. It was just a loan,
there's nothing more to it.

00:35:59.958 --> 00:36:02.958
He was in trouble,
there was no one else he could tell.

00:36:03.125 --> 00:36:04.792
So, what's your excuse?

00:36:04.917 --> 00:36:08.708
Sandy, I don't know
what Julie said to you.

00:36:08.917 --> 00:36:12.083
I'm trying to have a private
conversation with my wife.

00:36:17.083 --> 00:36:20.500
Two Mountain Dews, my good man.
Thank you. Ryan, greatest night ever.

00:36:20.667 --> 00:36:25.292
It's like those nights when the stars
and the cosmos and the moon align...

00:36:25.500 --> 00:36:28.375
...and it's just, like, wow.
Thank you. How's your mom doing?

00:36:29.083 --> 00:36:31.458
- High rolling. She was made for this place.
- Yeah?

00:36:31.583 --> 00:36:34.458
- Well, then maybe this could work.
- Yeah, maybe.

00:36:35.167 --> 00:36:37.750
Rabbit's foot? V Àmonos.

00:36:38.958 --> 00:36:41.958
By the end of the night,
she might know my first name.

00:36:42.458 --> 00:36:44.167
Duty calls.

00:36:51.500 --> 00:36:53.208
Look, I'm sorry.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:01.500
Hold up.

00:37:04.417 --> 00:37:06.708
- Oh, God.
- What the hell is your problem?

00:37:06.792 --> 00:37:10.292
What's my problem?
What's your problem? Back off.

00:37:11.583 --> 00:37:14.875
Ryan, I must have tripped.
It's these damn shoes.

00:37:17.292 --> 00:37:18.792
Hello?

00:37:25.875 --> 00:37:27.542
Here, good luck.

00:37:28.333 --> 00:37:31.833
- Dude, that lady is wasted.
- I bet you could bang her.

00:37:32.042 --> 00:37:33.625
Hey, shut up.

00:37:39.125 --> 00:37:42.708
Why don't you just quit staring
and help me up, okay? Get me up!

00:37:43.708 --> 00:37:45.417
Help me up!

00:37:45.625 --> 00:37:47.500
Finally. Jeez.

00:37:47.708 --> 00:37:50.125
Hey, Seth,
why don't you go get the car.

00:37:50.333 --> 00:37:52.417
- What, maybe you had one too many?
- No, I...

00:37:52.625 --> 00:37:54.917
What are you looking at?

00:37:55.125 --> 00:37:56.708
Where's Ryan? Ryan?

00:37:56.917 --> 00:37:59.000
Thanks, man. I'm right here, Mom.

00:37:59.083 --> 00:38:01.500
Ryan, honey, I'm so sorry.

00:38:01.583 --> 00:38:03.000
I ruined it, huh?

00:38:03.208 --> 00:38:07.583
- It's okay. We're almost there.
- No, no, I've ruined everything, huh?

00:38:08.583 --> 00:38:11.458
- You hate me.
- No, I don't.

00:38:11.542 --> 00:38:13.458
I love you, Mom.

00:38:13.667 --> 00:38:18.250
It's okay, everyone.
It's just a... It's a little accident.

00:38:18.542 --> 00:38:20.750
She's with us.

00:39:32.542 --> 00:39:34.375
You mind?

00:39:39.583 --> 00:39:42.792
So... You caught me.

00:39:42.958 --> 00:39:46.458
- You can't do this. You're his mother.
- I'm a mess, not a mother.

00:39:46.667 --> 00:39:49.458
- You have a responsibility.
- I'm being responsible.

00:39:51.458 --> 00:39:54.667
I'm not wired for this.

00:39:55.750 --> 00:39:58.667
I can't care for anybody else.

00:39:59.667 --> 00:40:01.250
I don't have what you got.

00:40:03.750 --> 00:40:08.542
The way your husband looks at you
and your kid looks at you.

00:40:09.042 --> 00:40:10.958
Even my kid.

00:40:13.042 --> 00:40:15.792
Like no matter what,
you're gonna make everything okay.

00:40:18.208 --> 00:40:20.583
You hold your family together.

00:40:21.708 --> 00:40:23.875
I tear mine apart.

00:40:24.583 --> 00:40:26.875
You can't walk away.

00:40:27.083 --> 00:40:28.667
Why?

00:40:30.167 --> 00:40:33.667
This will be the first good thing
I ever did for him.

00:40:36.958 --> 00:40:38.667
This way...

00:40:39.958 --> 00:40:41.375
...he ends up with a real mom.

00:40:44.958 --> 00:40:47.083
Take care of him, okay?

00:40:47.250 --> 00:40:48.958
He deserves it.

00:41:06.792 --> 00:41:08.292
Thanks.

00:41:54.833 --> 00:41:56.833
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:41:58.500 --> 00:42:01.292
- Where's...?
- Ryan's gonna stay with us now.

00:42:03.792 --> 00:42:05.625
That's awesome.

00:42:06.500 --> 00:42:09.292
I mean, that's...
That's awesome, right?

00:42:09.500 --> 00:42:12.792
Let's go talk about stuff. Come on.

00:42:20.250 --> 00:42:22.458
I'll unpack later.

00:42:34.125 --> 00:42:37.625
Well, there's a no-return policy now,
you know that.

00:42:40.042 --> 00:42:43.708
I love you. You know that?

00:42:45.542 --> 00:42:47.208
Are we okay?

00:42:47.417 --> 00:42:48.917
Yeah.

00:42:50.417 --> 00:42:52.000
Good.

00:42:53.208 --> 00:42:56.833
Because we just got in
way over our heads.

00:43:01.750 --> 00:43:05.875
So then she says, "Blow on these."
And clearly, she's talking about...
